cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use QFabric in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "QFabric: Quantum Network Emulation on FABRIC (QKD and entanglement over a P4 data plane)"
abstract: >-
  QFabric is a programmable quantum network emulation platform built on the
  FABRIC testbed. Fiber attenuation is emulated in a P4/BMv2 data plane as
  probabilistic drop of custom-EtherType photon frames, and BB84, decoy-state
  BB84, E91/BBM92, multi-hop entanglement swapping and a distributed gate run
  as real distributed processes across FABRIC nodes with full key
  distillation, cross-validated against the SeQUeNCe and NetSquid simulators
  on the same slice.
type: software
version: "0.2.0"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/kthare10/qfabric"
